{
  "_source": "Pathfinder RPG Bestiary, \"Table: Monster Statistics by CR\". Open Game Content under the Open Game License v1.0a. Transcribed from two independent OGL mirrors and cross-checked row-for-row.",
  "_pc_class_offset": "A creature with PC class levels has CR = character level - 1 (a 1st-level PC-classed NPC is CR 1/2). The scorer measures a generated character against the row for its level under that rule -- PF1e's own published offset, not a tuned correction.",
  "_extrapolation": "Published rows stop at CR 30; the generator's level band runs to 40, so rows CR 31-39 continue the table's own per-CR tail deltas (verified linear over CR 25-30) and carry \"extrapolated\": true. Never treat them as published.",
  "_target_multipliers": {
    "_why": "The bar-raising lever (Daniel's ruling, 2026-08-11): each benchmark denominator is multiplied by its axis's value before any ratio is computed, so holding generated NPCs ABOVE the published row -- the house feat surplus should beat a stock monster -- is an edit here, never an engine change (the build_archetypes.json precedent). All 1.0 until the post-repair baseline sets the real bar. Axes must exactly match the benchmarked set; gates/validate_power_metric.py fails loudly on a missing or misspelled one.",
